{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 3-5 EUR during the initial 10-day forecast horizon following a price drop, failing to capture the depth of the crash.",
    "Adjust for momentum lag: The model exhibits a significant lag in reacting to negative sentiment (value -1.00), predicting a flat or slightly rising trend while the market is in a steep downtrend.",
    "Reduce overshoot on recovery: After the price bottoms out (around day 10-12), the model underestimates the rebound magnitude, predicting a slow, linear recovery instead of the observed sharp V-shaped bounce.",
    "Incorporate sentiment volatility: Positive sentiment signals (0.20) are currently ignored by the model; forecasts should be adjusted upward immediately upon detection of positive sentiment to align with the subsequent price spike.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction: The model assumes a slow mean reversion to ~63 EUR; given the volatility, forecasts should be adjusted to reflect a faster reversion to the lower 56-58 EUR range before any upward correction."
  ]
}
